IMPORT prelude

§ `Set operators — Phase 1: SET OF a and the canonical vocabulary`

-- The §11.5 trichotomy of SET-OPERATORS-SPEC.md, executable. The legal
-- discriminator between readings of and/or is the extensional relationship
-- between the operand sets; each row of the trichotomy is just data.

§§ `Strings: the trichotomy`

-- Royal Trust [1986] UKPC 34: education ⊆ welfare, so the intersective
-- reading of "education and welfare" collapses to education and makes
-- "welfare" otiose.
`education purposes` MEANS setFromList (LIST "schools", "universities", "scholarships")
`welfare purposes`   MEANS setFromList (LIST "schools", "universities", "scholarships",
                                             "housing", "recreation")

#EVAL `education purposes` `is subset of` `welfare purposes`
#EVAL setSize (`education purposes` INTERSECT `welfare purposes`)

-- NY/NJ: disjoint operands, empty intersection — the union reading is forced
-- (the otiosity canon: Nam Hong [2016] SGCA 42 ¶26).
`new yorkers`   MEANS setFromList (LIST "alice", "bob")
`new jerseyans` MEANS setFromList (LIST "carol")

#EVAL setSize (`new yorkers` UNION `new jerseyans`)
#EVAL setSize (`new yorkers` INTERSECT `new jerseyans`)

-- Koh Lau Keow [2013] SGHC 155: co-extensive operands — the exegetical "or".
`home uses`      MEANS setFromList (LIST "refuge", "residence")
`sanctuary uses` MEANS setFromList (LIST "residence", "refuge")

#EVAL (`home uses` `is subset of` `sanctuary uses`) AND (`sanctuary uses` `is subset of` `home uses`)

-- Re Best [1904] 2 Ch 354: proper overlap — both terms do work, read literally.
`charitable objects` MEANS setFromList (LIST "almshouse", "school")
`benevolent objects` MEANS setFromList (LIST "school", "social club")

#EVAL setSize (`charitable objects` INTERSECT `benevolent objects`)

§§ `Difference: LESS and WITHOUT`

`all employees`  MEANS setFromList (LIST "dilbert", "alice", "wally", "asok")
`on probation`   MEANS setFromList (LIST "asok")

-- "all employees LESS those on probation" — backticked: bare LESS is a keyword
#EVAL setSize (`all employees` `LESS` `on probation`)
-- WITHOUT is the bare-spelling alias
#EVAL setSize (`all employees` WITHOUT `on probation`)

§§ `Enums: a finite element universe`

DECLARE State IS ONE OF NY, NJ, CT

`the tri-state universe` MEANS setFromList (LIST NY, NJ, CT)
`eligible states`        MEANS setFromList (LIST NY, NJ)

#EVAL NY `is in` `eligible states`
#EVAL CT `is in` `eligible states`
-- absolute complement, computable because the enum universe is finite
#EVAL setToList (`the tri-state universe` WITHOUT `eligible states`)

§§ `Construction and conversion`

#EVAL setSize (`new yorkers` INTERSECT emptySet)
#EVAL setSize (setFromList (LIST 1, 1, 2, 3, 3, 3))
#EVAL setToList (SET OF LIST 5, 5, 6)
